[Music]  contact tracing is underway this morning  for more than 200 people who may have  been exposed to the coronavirus at a new  jersey fundraiser  for president trump last week the  president traveled to the fundraiser  despite the white house knowing  before he left washington that a closed  aide had tested positive for the virus  a republican official tells cbs news  that the site was professionally cleaned  and sanitized  but it is still unclear how many guests  received a coronavirus test before the  event  new jersey's democratic governor phil  murphy joins us now governor murphy good  morning to you  i know you wish the president a speedy  recovery we wish the president a speedy  recovery  but we also hope for the continued  health and welfare of the people of new  jersey and that's where i want to begin  i'm curious what was your reaction when  you learned the president traveled to  your state  after learning that his close aide had  tested positive and what are your  biggest concerns now  good to be with you tony and i  underscore that we wish the president  and the first lady anybody who's been  infected a speedy recovery  that's very frustrating there's no other  way to put it  um we have paid an enormous price in new  jersey  uh with covid we've lost over 14 000  people  we've gotten things largely under  control but we're dealing with our own  spikes inside of our  four walls and to have a group  as they say the virus doesn't care who  you are new jersey doesn't care who you  are a group of folks from out of state  coming in knowingly having been exposed  to someone who's coveted positive  is really really frustrating it's  complicated we started the contact  tracing immediately  we ultimately got a list of the  attendees by mid-afternoon on friday  uh by the way it's a group of folks who  are nationally based not just  in new jersey we've got staff members of  the club  that we're contact tracing with here  we've done everything and we continue to  do everything we can we need more out of  the federal side of this  so governor but it's extremely  frustrating governor murphy uh  i also know it was frustrating that that  initial list of attendees did not  include phone numbers or addresses so it  was difficult to contact them  now that you are attempting to contact  them have you found any evidence of a  coveted spread  to the best of my knowledge no i was  just down with our health commissioner  this morning but there's a big but here  uh and you're you had a discussion just  prior to my coming on here  that addressed this it could be days uh  this  this virus takes a number of days to  incubate  uh so the notion of hey i just i got a  test after i heard this  and it came back negative so i could go  on my merry way that's not how this  works  anybody who was associated with that  fundraiser regardless of where they live  have got to take themselves off the  field you self-quarantine  first and foremost then after sort of  five to seven  days you get a test you still self  quarantine but you probably get another  test  but but you gotta take yourself off the  field exactly right governor murphy were  you given a heads up that there had been  an  issue in your state or did you hear  about it on the news like many of us did  yeah gail i did not get a heads up  unfortunately do you think you should  have gotten a heads up under the  circumstances  i think gail the thing that should have  happened is nobody should have come to  new jersey  that that trip should have been canceled  uh we're all doing  meetings virtually i'm doing fundraisers  we're all doing things that  allow us to have some amount of virtual  intimacy  that's what should have been done here  the the trip itself  was the wrong decision at every level  you know what i keep hearing that  we all wish the president and the first  lady a speedy recovery that's absolutely  true but i'm also hearing  people are angry that they're even put  in this position do you think the anger  is justified  and that maybe this will be a wake-up  call for even the president of the  united states  i think yes to both i think people have  a right to be upset and angry  uh particularly folks who have been  doing  all the right things every step of the  way  and secondly i hope it's a wake-up call  uh  and by the way we talk about this  chapter it's a law it's now a long book  with lots of chapters  of indoor behavior no face coverings  uh no social distancing that it can't go  on i hope to god  finally this gets through to everybody  uh no matter where you live no matter  what your party  that you've got to do the right thing  governor you said that this event should  not have happened  i'm curious the state has very strict  guidelines for who should come  what gatherings are okay i know as of  friday you were investigating whether  any social  distancing guidelines had been violated  by the president or his party  is that investigation ongoing what are  the findings  yes that would not come from my office  that would be a law enforcement matter  the attorney general  uh and and i there's a lot of attention  right now on the event i'll leave it at  that  uh part of this apparently was indoors  um  and so that's we all know the virus is a  lot more lethal  inside than it is outside um  but but this this entire uh event and  everything associated with it is  troubling  and it is being followed up on as best  we can and as aggressively as we can  here in new jersey i know you've been in  contact with your predecessor chris  christie who was also diagno  diagnosed with cobot what can you tell  us about how he's doing without breaking  any confidence  that the two of you share yeah we wish  the governor  and his first lady nothing but a speedy  recovery  the governor and i exchanged notes over  the weekend he knows we're here for him  beyond that i don't have any insights  it's been widely reported that he  as a precautionary matter checked  himself in to a hospital and and he is  in our prayers  uh as well all right governor murphy  thank you very much we appreciate you  being with us today  thank you tony thank you gail thank you

